&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;installation&#34;&gt;Installation
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;10
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;11
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# YOLO&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;curl -fsSL https://opencode.ai/v2/install &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; bash
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Package managers&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;npm i -g @opencode/cli@latest      &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# or bun/pnpm/yarn&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;brew install anomalyco/tap/opencode-v2 &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# macOS and Linux (recommended, always up to date)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;brew install opencode              &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# macOS and Linux (official brew formula, updated less)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;sudo pacman -S opencode            &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Arch Linux (Stable)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;paru -S opencode-beta              &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Arch Linux (Latest from AUR)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;mise use -g opencode               &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Any OS&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;nix run github:anomalyco/opencode  &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Nix&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[!TIP]
Remove versions older than 0.1.x before installing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;desktop-app-beta&#34;&gt;Desktop App (BETA)
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;OpenCode is also available as a desktop application. Download it from &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://opencode.ai/download&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;opencode.ai/download&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Platform&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Download&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;macOS (Apple Silicon)&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;opencode-desktop-mac-arm64.dmg&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;macOS (Intel)&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;opencode-desktop-mac-x64.dmg&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Windows&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;opencode-desktop-win-x64.exe&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Linux&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;.deb&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;.rpm&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;.AppImage&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# macOS (Homebrew)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;brew install --cask opencode-desktop
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id=&#34;installation-directory&#34;&gt;Installation Directory
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;The install script respects the following priority order for the installation path:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;$OPENCODE_INSTALL_DIR&lt;/code&gt; - Custom installation directory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;$XDG_BIN_DIR&lt;/code&gt; - XDG Base Directory Specification compliant path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;$HOME/bin&lt;/code&gt; - Standard user binary directory (if it exists or can be created)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;$HOME/.opencode/bin&lt;/code&gt; - Default fallback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Examples&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nv&#34;&gt;OPENCODE_INSTALL_DIR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;/usr/local/bin curl -fsSL https://opencode.ai/v2/install &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; bash
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nv&#34;&gt;XDG_BIN_DIR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nv&#34;&gt;$HOME&lt;/span&gt;/.local/bin curl -fsSL https://opencode.ai/v2/install &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; bash
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;agents&#34;&gt;Agents
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;OpenCode includes two built-in agents you can switch between with the &lt;code&gt;Tab&lt;/code&gt; key.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;build&lt;/strong&gt; - Default, full-access agent for development work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;plan&lt;/strong&gt; - Read-only agent for analysis and code exploration
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Denies file edits by default&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Asks permission before running bash commands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideal for exploring unfamiliar codebases or planning changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also included is a &lt;strong&gt;general&lt;/strong&gt; subagent for complex searches and multistep tasks.
This is used internally and can be invoked using &lt;code&gt;@general&lt;/code&gt; in messages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://opencode.ai/docs/agents&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;agents&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;documentation&#34;&gt;Documentation
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;For more info on how to configure OpenCode, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://opencode.ai/docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;head over to our docs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;contributing&#34;&gt;Contributing
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;re interested in contributing to OpenCode, please read our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;./CONTRIBUTING.md&#34; &gt;contributing docs&lt;/a&gt; before submitting a pull request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;building-on-opencode&#34;&gt;Building on OpenCode
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you are working on a project that&amp;rsquo;s related to OpenCode and is using &amp;ldquo;opencode&amp;rdquo; as part of its name, for example &amp;ldquo;opencode-dashboard&amp;rdquo; or &amp;ldquo;opencode-mobile&amp;rdquo;, please add a note to your README to clarify that it is not built by the OpenCode team and is not affiliated with us in any way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join our community&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://discord.gg/opencode&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Discord&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://x.com/opencode&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;X.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
